  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certifies that on 20th July 2006, the erection of a single storey rear extension, with dimensions 1.80m wide, 3.90m deep, and 2.85m high, returning a volume of 20.00m3, giving a total volume increase to the original house of 38.35m3, as shown on drawing numbers 705-P02 & 705-P04, received 20th July 2006, was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nFollowing the proposed extensions consisting of the erection of a single storey rear extension, the resulting building would fall within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995.\r\n"
